hint.txt:
    A C++ command-line program (C++17), built with CMake (3.14 or later), with unit tests in GoogleTest.
    - Layout: put the program's logic in a small static library inside the project, with its public header under include/{{NAME_SNAKE}}/, and keep src/main.cpp thin, so the GoogleTest tests call the logic directly. Put everything in namespace {{NAME_SNAKE}}. Use {{NAME_SNAKE}} for C++ identifiers, the namespace, header and source names and include guards, and {{NAME}} for the executable and the CMake project.
    - The program prints "{{NAME}}: placeholder - nothing implemented yet", supports --help and --version (printing "{{NAME}} 0.1.0", from the CMake project version), and an unknown option prints the usage to stderr and exits with status 2.
    - GoogleTest is required for the tests: a CMake option {{NAME_SNAKE}}_BUILD_TESTS, on by default. When it's on, use an installed GoogleTest from find_package(GTest), or download GoogleTest 1.15.2 with FetchContent (URL https://github.com/google/googletest/releases/download/v1.15.2/googletest-1.15.2.tar.gz, URL_HASH SHA256=7b42b4d6ed48810c5362c265a17faebe90dc2373c885e5216439d37927f02926) only when the developer opts in with {{NAME_SNAKE}}_FETCH_GOOGLETEST, off by default. With neither, configuring fails with a message saying how to install GoogleTest, opt in to the download, or turn the tests off with -D{{NAME_SNAKE}}_BUILD_TESTS=OFF. Register the tests with gtest_discover_tests.
    - tests/smoke.sh: configure and build in a temporary build folder (never in the source tree) with -D{{NAME_SNAKE}}_FETCH_GOOGLETEST=OFF and -DFETCHCONTENT_FULLY_DISCONNECTED=ON, run the program, check its placeholder line, --help, --version and that an unknown option fails, and always run ctest. Never download anything. Work with Apple clang on macOS and with gcc on Linux.
    - Warnings (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic) on for gcc and clang, without failing the build.
    - README: building, running, testing, how to get GoogleTest (Homebrew, apt, or the opt-in download), and the choices made.
    GoogleTest is installed here, so --check-type builds and runs the tests.

